 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nSignal validation removed causing signals to extend beyond message boundaries\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen creating CAN messages with signals that extend beyond the message length, the validation that should prevent this is no longer working. Signals can now be added to messages even when they don't fit within the message boundaries.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport cantools\n\n# Create a signal that extends beyond message boundaries\nsignal = cantools.database.can.Signal('S', 7, 33, 'big_endian')  # 33-bit signal\nmessage = cantools.database.can.Message(37, 'M', 4, [signal], strict=False)  # 4-byte message\n\n# This should raise an error but doesn't\ndb = cantools.database.can.Database([message])\n```\n\nExpected behavior: Should raise `cantools.database.errors.Error` with message \"The signal S does not fit in message M.\"\n\nActual behavior: No error is raised, allowing invalid signal configurations.\n\nThis also affects loading database files with invalid signal configurations - files that should be rejected in strict mode are now accepted.\n</issue>\n",
